# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Volleyball Tracker — environment variables (client app)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The app is offline-first: cloud sync is manual, from Settings > Cloud Sync,
# never automatic. See docs/SYNC_PROTOCOL.md for the sync design and
# server/README.md for the NestJS API + MySQL/Hostinger + Railway setup.
#
# To ship a default connection baked into the app (so a fresh install already
# points at your Railway-hosted API instead of starting fully local):
#   cp .env.example .env
# `.env` is covered by .gitignore's local-env-file pattern — never commit it.
#
# This default is just a starting point: Settings > Cloud Sync lets a user
# point the app at a different API, or clear the connection entirely to go
# fully local-only, from within the app itself. See connectionStore.ts.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Anything prefixed EXPO_PUBLIC_ is compiled into the client JS bundle and
# is NOT secret from someone who decompiles the app. That's fine here — this
# is the shared static API key documented in docs/SYNC_PROTOCOL.md, not a
# database credential (the database credentials live only in server/.env,
# server-side, never in this file).

# Base URL of the deployed NestJS sync API (e.g. your Railway app URL).
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://your-app.up.railway.app

# Must match API_KEY in server/.env on the deployed API.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_KEY=
